if time allows before May 25\"\n\n  # --- D049 Tier 3 ---\n  - plan_id: P033\n    name: Grammar-only cross-model validation (Qwen/Llama EE)\n    claim: C3_composable_framework\n    priority: 3\n    depends_on: null\n    description: \"Grammar-only ablation on Qwen/Llama WikiEvents EE for completeness\"\n\n  - plan_id: P034\n    name: Bootstrap CI for EE metrics\n    claim: C6_f1_impact\n    priority: 3\n    depends_on: null\n    description: \"Statistical significance for EE F1 changes\"\n\n  - plan_id: P035\n    name: Latency overhead measurement\n    claim: C3_composable_framework\n    priority: 3\n    depends_on: null\n    description: \"Wall-clock comparison: unconstrained vs constrained decoding overhead\"\n\ngpu_budget:\n  allocated: \"westd-16980 cuda:0,1 + westd-21461 cuda:0,1 (4x RTX PRO 6000 96GB)\"\n  total_used: \"~45 GPU-hours (RE + WikiEvents EE complete)\"\n  status: \"70B experiments next — 4 GPUs all allocated for 70B SciERC/DocRED parallel runs\"\n","numLines":57,"startLine":258,"totalLines":314}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011SCuv5gzkan9Gv6sAsom6J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the complete experiment plan. Let me identify which experiments need predictions:\n\n**Completed (actual data in registry):**\n- P001-P020 (Phase 0, Phase 2 SciERC/DocRED, Cross-Model, Supplementary)\n- P021-P028 (WikiEvents EE)\n- P029 (70B SciERC — DONE)\n\n**RUNNING:**\n- P030 (70B DocRED unconstrained + constrained)\n- P035 (Latency overhead — partially: SciERC done, DocRED running)\n\n\n- P031-P034 (Error analysis, EE FT composability, Grammar-only cross-model EE, Bootstrap CI for EE)\n\nI need to generate the comprehensive YAML with predictions for all experiments—using actual registry data for completed ones and well-reasoned estimates for the running and planned ones based on the patterns I'm seeing across the results.\n\nGenerating the YAML output... Looking at the performance ratios between model sizes, I'm seeing that 70B tends to perform roughly half as well on SciERC compared to 8B Llama, so applying that same ratio to DocRED's 8B baseline of 26.07% gives me around 12.8% — though DocRED's tight constraints and 96 relations might limit how much improvement I can actually achieve, so I'm predicting closer to 11% for the unconstrained case. For the relation violation metric, the 70B should handle memorization significantly better than the 8B baseline of 16.03%.\n\nFor the constrained scenario, the larger model's lower relation violation rate of around 5% means fewer latent violations surface through the grammar, pushing the defect rate down to roughly 1.0-1.5%. That represents about an 89% reduction from the unconstrained 11%, and the relation F1 delta should stay nearly neutral at around +0.2 percentage points.\n\nNow I'm ready to compile these predictions into the final YAML output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_